                  "explanation": "Both Medicare Advantage (since the original Balanced Budget Act 1997 and refined under various CMS rulemaking) and Medicaid managed care (under the 2016 Medicaid Managed Care Final Rule, 42 CFR 438.68) have federal network adequacy requirements. These specify time/distance standards (e.g., PCP within 30 minutes/30 miles, specialists within 60 minutes/60 miles). Standards apply to BOTH primary care AND specialists, plus hospitals, behavioral health, pharmacy, etc. Plans must demonstrate compliance for contract renewal. The 2024 MA Final Rule strengthened MA network adequacy requirements significantly.",
